course: dictionary
lesson: 8661
title: Seaweed and the sea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Seaweed is a plant-like living thing that grows in the sea. It is often green, brown or red, and it sticks to rocks. You can find it on the beach, especially in rock pools.
explain: The sentence «Picture a beach after a storm: among the seaweed lies a black leathery pouch» gives you clues. Seaweed lies among things on the beach, so it is something the sea leaves on the sand and rocks. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Some words name a whole group, and others name one kind inside it. In «sea urchins eat kelp seaweed», kelp is one kind of seaweed. Seaweeds is the word for more than one kind.
fact: Seaweed is a plant-like living thing that grows in the sea.
fact: Seaweed is often green, brown or red, and it sticks to rocks.
fact: «A strand of seaweed» and «a piece of seaweed» are common phrases.
fact: Scientists say seaweed is a kind of algae, not a true plant with roots and flowers, but it makes food from sunlight.
fact: Seaweed is also used as food in many countries, for example in sushi and some snacks.
exercise: «Picture a beach after a storm: among the seaweed lies a black leathery pouch.» Where does the seaweed lie? | *On the beach | Under a mountain | Inside a cow's stomach | In the sky
exercise: What is seaweed? | A stone that sits at the bottom of a river | A kind of bird with long legs | *A plant-like living thing that grows in the sea | A metal that goes rusty
exercise: «Sea otters eat sea urchins, and sea urchins eat kelp seaweed.» Find and copy one word that names a kind of seaweed. | sea | *kelp | otters | urchins
test: Which of these is true about seaweed? | It has teeth and eats fish | *It grows in the sea and often sticks to rocks | It is always bright blue | It flies through the air like a bird
test: «A mermaid's purse is the egg case of a catshark; curly tendrils at its four corners hold it to seaweed.» What do the tendrils do? | They eat the seaweed | They make the purse float away | *They hold the purse to the seaweed | They turn the purse into a fish
exam: Which of these is a use of seaweed given in the lessons? | Fuel for cars | Writing paper | Building bricks | *Food, for example in sushi
